C13B.bank02 = {"1":{"name":"Pioneer","tags":"INITIATIVE \u00b7 START \u00b7 DECIDE","core":"Today pushes toward initiative. It favors the first move, the clean decision, and the thing that needs somebody to stop waiting and begin.","openers":["Today runs on first-move energy. Something gets easier once somebody actually starts it.","Today favors initiative. Pick the direction, make the call, and give the day something to move behind.","This is a start-it day. Momentum matters more than waiting for perfect certainty.","The day rewards clean independence. Use your own judgment before the room fills your head with everybody else's."],"light":["Starting has more value than over-preparing.","A direct decision can clear hours of hesitation.","Original approaches have room to work today.","Leadership is useful when it creates movement instead of attention.","Independent work can move quickly when the goal is clear.","A stalled situation may only need somebody willing to go first.","Confidence is productive when it stays connected to reality.","The clean version of this day turns personal will into forward motion."],"watch":["Initiative can turn into picking a fight just to prove you cannot be controlled.","Impatience makes other people's pace feel more annoying than it needs to.","A strong opinion can become a refusal to listen.","Starting five things is not the same as moving one thing forward.","Pride can make a simple correction feel like losing.","The urge to lead can become the urge to dominate.","Doing everything alone can create problems that cooperation would have prevented.","Watch random arguments. Not every disagreement needs to become a test of strength."],"anchors":{"best":"initiate, decide, pitch, begin, take ownership.","watch":"ego contests, impatience, unnecessary arguments, refusing useful help.","question":"What am I waiting for permission to start?"}},"3":{"name":"Storyteller","tags":"EXPRESSION \u00b7 PEOPLE \u00b7 CREATIVITY","core":"Today opens the channel for expression. Conversation, humor, creativity, visibility, and social movement can carry more weight than usual.","openers":["Today runs on expressive energy. Say it, show it, make it easier for people to feel what you mean.","This is a communication day. The right words can move something that force would only make heavier.","Today wants movement through expression. Create, talk, pitch, write, perform, or bring some life back into the room.","The day gets stronger when ideas leave your head and become something other people can actually see or hear."],"light":["Creative work has more room to breathe.","Conversation can unlock stuck situations.","Humor can lower tension when it is not being used to dodge the truth.","Visibility helps when there is something real behind it.","Social energy can create useful connections.","A message lands better when it has personality.","Play can produce better ideas than forcing seriousness.","The clean version of this day turns expression into connection."],"watch":["Scattered attention can eat the whole day.","Talking about the work can replace doing the work.","Gossip and exaggeration create mess faster than they create excitement.","A need for attention can distort what actually needs to be said.","Too many ideas can leave nothing finished.","Jokes can become an escape hatch from a serious conversation.","Mood swings can make the day feel more dramatic than the facts support.","Watch getting scattered. Pick a lane long enough to make something real."],"anchors":{"best":"communicate, create, socialize, present, write, brainstorm.","watch":"distraction, gossip, exaggeration, unfinished work, performing instead of dealing.","question":"What needs to be expressed clearly instead of carried around?"}},"4":{"name":"Builder","tags":"STRUCTURE \u00b7 WORK \u00b7 FOLLOW-THROUGH","core":"Today favors structure. Plans matter, but only if they turn into real work. This is the kind of day that rewards steady execution, cleanup, maintenance, and finishing what has been left loose.","openers":["Today runs on builder energy. Put the pieces in order and make something solid.","This is a work-the-plan day. Structure helps, but the point is to actually execute it.","Today rewards steady progress. Slow, correct work beats rushed work that has to be done twice.","The day wants something tangible by the end of it. Organize it, repair it, finish it, or build it properly."],"light":["Routine can create momentum instead of boredom.","Detailed work is easier to respect today.","Cleaning up loose ends creates real relief.","A realistic plan can turn pressure into steps.","Reliability matters more than flash.","Maintenance prevents future problems.","Boundaries and schedules can protect attention.","The clean version of this day turns structure into visible progress."],"watch":["Planning can become procrastination with better stationery.","Rigidity makes every interruption feel like a threat.","Perfectionism can slow a simple task into the ground.","Overwork can turn discipline into exhaustion.","A rule can keep being followed after it stops helping.","Control gets tighter when the plan starts slipping.","Mess or lateness may irritate you more than the situation deserves.","Do the work, not just the plan."],"anchors":{"best":"organize, repair, budget, schedule, complete, build systems.","watch":"rigidity, micromanaging, perfectionism, shortcuts, working yourself empty.","question":"What would make today feel more solid by tonight?"}},"5":{"name":"Explorer","tags":"CHANGE \u00b7 MOVEMENT \u00b7 EXPERIENCE","core":"Today wants movement. Variety, travel, social contact, experimentation, and a break from stale routines can open doors that sitting still will not.","openers":["Today runs on movement. Change the scenery, try the different route, and give yourself something new to respond to.","This is an experience day. You learn more by getting into the world than by thinking about it from the same chair.","Today favors flexibility. The plan may change, and that can be useful instead of annoying.","The day gets better when there is room for discovery. Move, meet people, test something, or shake up the routine."],"light":["Adaptability is an advantage today.","A new environment can change your thinking quickly.","Social movement can create unexpected openings.","Experimentation is useful when the stakes allow it.","Curiosity can solve a problem that routine could not.","Travel and exploration fit the tone of the day.","A flexible schedule may outperform a rigid one.","The clean version of this day turns change into useful experience."],"watch":["Restlessness can make a good situation look broken just because it feels familiar.","Impulse can outrun consequence.","Too much stimulation can scatter the whole day.","Quick pleasure can become an easy distraction.","Commitments may feel heavier than they really are.","Running from an uncomfortable conversation does not make it disappear.","Change for its own sake can create cleanup tomorrow.","Get out, travel, be social, but do not confuse motion with progress."],"anchors":{"best":"explore, travel, socialize, experiment, adapt, try something new.","watch":"impulsiveness, escapism, overindulgence, needless disruption, dodging responsibility.","question":"What needs fresh movement, and what only needs patience?"}},"6":{"name":"Caretaker","tags":"HOME \u00b7 FAMILY \u00b7 RESPONSIBILITY","core":"Today pulls attention toward people, home, responsibility, care, repair, and the quality of the environment around you. It favors showing up in ways that are useful, warm, and real.","openers":["Today runs on caretaker energy. Give attention to the people and places that actually depend on you.","This is a home-and-responsibility day. Handle what needs care instead of assuming somebody else will.","Today favors repair. A conversation, a room, a relationship, or a responsibility may need your actual presence.","The day gets stronger when care becomes practical. Show up, help, teach, clean up, or make the space better."],"light":["Family time can matter more than another hour of productivity.","Practical support lands well today.","Home projects can create emotional relief.","Teaching and guidance are useful when they are invited.","Beauty and comfort can change the tone of a space.","Responsibility feels lighter when it is shared clearly.","A neglected relationship may benefit from real attention.","The clean version of this day turns care into stability."],"watch":["Helping can turn into interfering.","You may volunteer for too much and resent it later.","Perfectionism can make the people around you feel managed.","Worry can disguise itself as control.","Other people's problems can swallow your own priorities.","Guilt can make saying no feel harsher than it is.","Trying to fix somebody who did not ask can create the exact tension you wanted to prevent.","Spend real time with family. Do not turn care into control."],"anchors":{"best":"family, home, repair, support, teaching, beautifying, responsible follow-through.","watch":"martyrdom, meddling, guilt, over-responsibility, perfectionism.","question":"Who or what actually needs care from me today, and what is not mine to carry?"}},"7":{"name":"Seeker","tags":"SCRUTINY \u00b7 QUIET \u00b7 BODY CHECK","core":"Today slows the surface down and turns attention inward. Research, solitude, analysis, reflection, and careful observation fit the energy. Code13 treats 7 more cautiously than generic numerology does.","openers":["Today runs on seeker energy. Slow the noise down and look closer before you commit to the obvious answer.","This is a scrutiny day. Read the fine print, listen to your body, and give yourself enough quiet to notice what you have been missing.","Today favors depth over volume. Fewer inputs and better questions will get you further.","The day wants observation before reaction. Study it, check it, and do not force certainty where you do not have it."],"light":["Quiet can reveal what constant input has been covering up.","Research and review are productive today.","A solo walk or focused study session can reset your thinking.","Details deserve a second look.","Intuition is more useful when it survives scrutiny.","Rest can be productive when the body is asking for it.","You may catch a flaw before it becomes a bigger problem.","The clean version of this day turns scrutiny into insight."],"watch":["Overthinking can turn one concern into ten imaginary ones.","Isolation can make perspective worse instead of better.","Suspicion can create distance from people who have not actually done anything wrong.","The mind can keep working long after the body needs a break.","A quiet mood can slide into heaviness if you feed it with more noise inside your own head.","Analysis can delay a decision that already has enough information.","Ignoring physical warning signs is especially unwise in the Code13 7 pattern.","Watch your body. The house system treats 7 days as carrying a real risk of getting sick or hurt."],"anchors":{"best":"research, study, review, rest, journal, inspect, spend time alone.","watch":"overthinking, suspicion, isolation, ignoring physical signals, forcing social energy.","question":"What gets clearer if I stop adding noise to it?"}},"8":{"name":"Executive","tags":"MONEY \u00b7 EXECUTION \u00b7 CONSEQUENCE","core":"Today puts material reality on the table. Money, authority, negotiation, business, consequence, and measurable results matter more. Code13 treats 8 as one of the primary wealth energies.","openers":["Today runs on executive energy. Make the decision that improves the actual numbers, not just the appearance of progress.","This is a money-and-execution day. Deals, budgets, pricing, business, and material decisions deserve attention.","Today favors leverage. Put effort where it can create a measurable return.","The day wants results. Handle the financial or operational move you have been avoiding."],"light":["Business decisions can benefit from clear thinking today.","Money deserves direct attention instead of avoidance.","Negotiation can move when the terms are concrete.","Leadership works when responsibility stays attached to authority.","A hard decision may be easier when the outcome is measurable.","Long-term material planning fits the day.","Effort can convert into visible results.","The clean version of this day uses power without cutting ethical corners."],"watch":["Greed can disguise itself as ambition.","A money decision made only to prove something can become expensive.","Control can create unnecessary resistance.","Status can distract from actual value.","Winning the negotiation is not useful if the deal itself is bad.","Pressure can make people feel like tools instead of people.","Material focus can become tunnel vision.","Make money moves, but no ethical corners."],"anchors":{"best":"money, business, pricing, negotiation, leadership, execution, resource decisions.","watch":"greed, control, ego spending, unethical shortcuts, treating every interaction like a transaction.","question":"What material move creates real value instead of just looking powerful?"}},"9":{"name":"Mirror","tags":"RELEASE \u00b7 ADAPT \u00b7 COMPLETE","core":"Today favors completion, release, adjustment, and reading what the situation is actually showing you. The Code13 9 is the Mirror. It adapts, reflects, and knows when forcing the old shape is no longer useful.","openers":["Today runs on mirror energy. Pay attention to what the situation is showing back to you and adjust accordingly.","This is a release-and-adapt day. Finish what is ready to finish instead of forcing another chapter out of it.","Today favors flexibility around endings. Something may work better once you stop demanding that it stay the same.","The day asks for perspective. Read the room, complete the cycle, and let the dead weight go."],"light":["Finishing can create more momentum than starting something new.","Adaptation helps when conditions have genuinely changed.","Old emotional residue can be cleared instead of carried forward.","A conversation may improve when you reflect what is actually happening instead of defending a fixed position.","Different types of people may be easier to understand today.","Closure can be practical, not dramatic.","Letting go can free attention for what is still alive.","The clean version of this day turns reflection into adjustment."],"watch":["Holding onto an expired situation wastes energy.","Mirroring everybody else can make your own position hard to find.","Understanding why something happened can become an excuse not to end it.","Emotional residue can make the present look like the past.","Trying to force an outcome fights the basic rhythm of the day.","Adapting too much can become self-erasure.","Nostalgia can make a closed chapter look more useful than it was.","Release and adapt. Do not force it."],"anchors":{"best":"finish, release, forgive where appropriate, clear clutter, adapt, close loops.","watch":"forcing outcomes, carrying old baggage, people-pleasing, losing your own position, reopening finished chapters.","question":"What is already over that I am still spending energy trying to keep alive?"}},"11":{"name":"Antenna","tags":"EMOTIONAL INTENSITY \u00b7 SIGNAL \u00b7 GROUNDING","core":"Today carries more emotional and intuitive voltage. Ideas can hit fast, feelings can hit hard, and subtle things can feel louder. Code13 treats 11 as emotionally intense and potentially unstable when it is not grounded.","openers":["Today runs on high-voltage energy. Pay attention to what hits you, but ground it before you build a whole story around it.","This is an emotionally intense day. Strong ideas and strong feelings can both arrive fast.","Today can sharpen intuition and sensitivity at the same time. Keep the signal. Lose the panic.","The day turns the volume up. That can mean inspiration, overwhelm, or both, depending on how grounded you stay."],"light":["Sudden ideas can be worth capturing.","Creative or intuitive connections may arrive quickly.","A meaningful conversation can cut through surface-level noise.","Sensitivity can reveal what has been overlooked.","Inspiration has more value when written down and tested later.","Quiet grounding can make the useful signal easier to separate from emotional static.","You may understand the emotional core of something faster than usual.","The clean version of this day turns intensity into insight."],"watch":["A strong feeling can become a false certainty.","Anxiety can make every signal look urgent.","Too much caffeine, noise, conflict, or stimulation can push the nervous system too far.","Overthinking small details can drain the useful part of the day.","Idealism can make ordinary reality feel disappointing.","Emotional crashes are more likely when intensity is treated like endless fuel.","Not every coincidence needs an explanation.","Watch for emotionally crashing out. Ground the feeling first."],"anchors":{"best":"capture ideas, create, reflect, have meaningful conversations, ground, notice patterns without worshipping them.","watch":"anxiety, overstimulation, emotional certainty, caffeine-fueled spirals, burnout.","question":"What still feels true after my body calms down?"}},"22":{"name":"Master Builder","tags":"MASTER BUILDING \u00b7 SCALE \u00b7 SYSTEMS","core":"Today favors large-scale building when the foundation is real. Vision has to survive logistics. The best use of 22 is taking something ambitious and giving it structure, sequence, resources, and a path into reality.","openers":["Today runs on master-builder energy. Think big, then give the big idea an actual structure.","This is a scale day. The vision matters, but the next practical step matters just as much.","Today favors systems, long-range planning, and work that has to hold up beyond the moment.","The day asks whether the idea can carry real weight. Build the foundation, not just the pitch."],"light":["Complex projects can be easier to see as systems.","Long-term planning has more value today.","A big goal can become less intimidating once it is broken into real stages.","Coordination and infrastructure matter.","The right practical decision can protect a much larger vision.","Work with lasting impact fits the tone of the day.","High standards are useful when they improve the structure instead of freezing it.","The clean version of this day turns scale into something buildable."],"watch":["The size of the goal can create paralysis.","Perfectionism can make the first step feel insultingly small.","Control can tighten when too many moving pieces feel uncertain.","People can become secondary to the plan.","Overwork can make the body pay for the ambition.","A huge vision can become an excuse not to finish the next concrete task.","Pressure can make ordinary progress feel like failure.","Do not let the scale of the plan stop the work that actually builds it."],"anchors":{"best":"systems, infrastructure, long-range plans, major projects, coordination, durable work.","watch":"paralysis, perfectionism, control, treating people like resources, ignoring the body.","question":"What is the smallest real step that makes the big plan more structurally possible?"}},"28":{"name":"Wealth-Builder","tags":"WEALTH \u00b7 EFFORT \u00b7 MATERIAL GAIN","core":"28 is a fixed Code13 wealth pattern. The supported doctrine is direct: effort can convert into material gain. Greed is the shadow. This bank stays narrow where the source stays narrow.","openers":["Today carries wealth-builder energy. Put effort where there is a real path to material return.","This is an effort-to-gain day. Focus on useful work, value exchange, and the move that can produce a tangible result.","Today favors material progress when the work underneath it is real.","The day puts value on the table. Build, earn, negotiate, or improve the thing that can actually pay back effort."],"light":["Useful effort deserves a measurable target.","Material decisions benefit from clear value exchange.","Work that improves earning power fits the day.","A practical financial move can matter more than symbolic progress.","The clean pattern connects gain to effort.","Tangible results are the point, not appearance."],"watch":["Greed is the standing shadow.","More can become the goal even after more stops improving anything.","A shortcut can corrupt the value exchange underneath the gain.","Material appetite can outrun judgment.","The pursuit of profit can become detached from usefulness.","If gain is the only measure, there is no natural stopping point."],"anchors":{"best":"earning, pricing, improving value, monetizing useful work, material planning.","watch":"greed, exploitative shortcuts, chasing more without a target, confusing price with value.","question":"Where can real effort create real material return without corrupting the exchange?"}},"33":{"name":"Guardian","tags":"INFLUENCE \u00b7 CARE \u00b7 GUIDANCE","core":"Today puts influence and responsibility together. The energy favors teaching, protecting, guiding, and using your voice in a way that leaves people steadier rather than more dependent on you.","openers":["Today runs on guardian energy. Use your influence to steady something, teach something, or help somebody stand stronger.","This is an influence-through-care day. What you say can carry weight, so make sure the weight is useful.","Today favors guidance with boundaries. Help without turning yourself into the entire support system.","The day asks for responsible influence. Lead with care, but leave other people room to own their choices."],"light":["Teaching can land deeply today.","A calm voice can stabilize a difficult situation.","Support is strongest when it restores somebody else's agency.","Creative influence can carry a protective tone.","Service can feel meaningful when it is chosen rather than guilt-driven.","People may be more receptive to guidance that is warm and practical.","A difficult emotional situation can benefit from steadiness.","The clean version of this day uses influence to strengthen, not control."],"watch":["Helping can become rescuing.","Guilt can turn a voluntary sacrifice into resentment.","Taking on everybody's pain can overwhelm the day.","High ideals can become judgment toward imperfect people.","Being needed can become emotionally addictive.","The desire to protect can make boundaries blurry.","Public responsibility can crowd out the people closest to you.","Do not carry somebody else's entire life just because you can see how to help."],"anchors":{"best":"teach, mentor, support, guide, create something uplifting, protect what genuinely needs protection.","watch":"martyrdom, rescuing, guilt, over-responsibility, emotional absorption.","question":"How can I help in a way that leaves the other person stronger, not more dependent?"}}};
C13B.bank03 = {"1":{"dos":["Start the project, task, or hobby you've been putting off.","Wear or choose something that makes you feel visible instead of blending in.","Make one important decision using your own judgment first.","Be the first person to speak up when something needs to be said.","Move your body hard enough to wake yourself up and create momentum.","Send the message, application, pitch, or request you have been hesitating to send.","Choose one priority and take ownership of getting it moving.","Fix one situation where waiting on everybody else's opinion has stalled you.","Put your name on an idea instead of hiding behind the group.","Do the hardest first step before you start polishing the easy parts.","Take a small calculated risk that moves you toward something you actually want.","Set one boundary clearly instead of hoping somebody notices it.","End the day with one thing that exists because you decided to begin it."],"donts":["Don't wait around for somebody else to give you permission.","Don't copy somebody else's move just because they made it first.","Don't make yourself smaller just to keep other people comfortable.","Don't burn the day scrolling when you know there is something you need to begin.","Don't let an old mistake decide what you are willing to try next.","Don't start an argument just because somebody challenged your opinion.","Don't reject useful help only because you want the win to be completely yours.","Don't confuse being first with being right.","Don't start five new things and leave all five half-built.","Don't turn a delay into proof that the whole plan is failing.","Don't make a reckless decision just to prove you are fearless.","Don't bulldoze quieter people when leadership would work better.","Don't spend the whole day talking about what you are going to do."]},"3":{"dos":["Make something for the fun of making it: write, draw, perform, design, or create.","Tell the story, make the joke, or say the thing that brings some life into the room.","Wear or use something expressive instead of defaulting to boring.","Call somebody you actually enjoy talking to and have a real conversation.","Give yourself some room to play. Not every useful idea has to arrive through pressure.","Write down three ideas before judging whether any of them are good.","Turn one boring message or presentation into something people will actually remember.","Share something you made instead of keeping every creative idea private.","Use humor to lower tension without using it to avoid the real point.","Finish one small creative piece today, even if it is not perfect.","Ask a question that gets somebody talking instead of keeping the conversation on autopilot.","Change the atmosphere around you with music, design, words, or movement.","Say the honest thing in language the other person can actually hear."],"donts":["Don't spend the day gossiping or passing around somebody else's business.","Don't bury a creative idea just because it feels silly at first.","Don't turn a simple thing into a giant problem because the details are boring you.","Don't hide something you're good at because you're scared of being judged.","Don't make everything heavy today. Serious does not automatically mean important.","Don't confuse talking about the work with finishing the work.","Don't chase attention with a story you know is exaggerated.","Don't make a joke out of something that actually needs an honest conversation.","Don't open ten creative tabs and complete none of them.","Don't let one critical comment erase all the positive evidence around your work.","Don't promise more than you can deliver because the moment feels exciting.","Don't use social energy as an excuse to avoid being alone with your own thoughts.","Don't let your mood decide that every unfinished idea deserves to be abandoned."]},"4":{"dos":["Clean and organize one space you actually use every day.","Put the budget, schedule, or task list somewhere you can see it and follow it.","Do something grounding that gets you out of your head and back into your body.","Finish the difficult task you've been avoiding before adding another one.","Double-check the timing, details, and logistics before you call the job done.","Repair one small thing before it turns into a bigger problem.","Break one overwhelming job into steps you can actually complete.","Pay a bill, file a document, schedule an appointment, or handle one boring responsibility.","Set up tomorrow so you are not creating unnecessary chaos for yourself.","Choose quality over speed on the task that needs to last.","Create one repeatable system for something you keep doing the hard way.","Show up on time for the thing you said you would do.","Leave one part of your life more stable tonight than it was this morning."],"donts":["Don't let your space become a mess and pretend it is not affecting you.","Don't take lazy shortcuts on work that actually matters.","Don't reject a useful suggestion just because it was not part of your original plan.","Don't spend money carelessly on something you do not need.","Don't turn discipline into punishment by working until you are useless.","Don't spend three hours perfecting a plan you could have started in thirty minutes.","Don't micromanage somebody who is already handling their responsibility.","Don't treat a changed schedule like a personal attack.","Don't keep a rule just because it used to work.","Don't confuse being busy with making progress.","Don't delay a simple repair because it is annoying.","Don't punish yourself for resting after the important work is handled.","Don't make the whole day rigid enough that one surprise ruins it."]},"5":{"dos":["Change the route, the setting, or the routine enough to give your brain something new.","Try a food, place, activity, or experience you normally would not pick.","Leave some room for spontaneity instead of scheduling every inch of the day.","Talk to somebody new or somebody whose world is different from yours.","Get your body moving. Dance, walk, train, travel - do something that breaks the stale energy.","Work somewhere different if the usual environment has gone dead.","Test a new method before deciding the old method is the only one that works.","Say yes to one low-risk experience that expands your normal range.","Use a change in plans as information instead of immediately fighting it.","Learn something by doing it instead of reading about it for another hour.","Take a short trip, errand, or walk that gets you into a different environment.","Meet somebody halfway instead of demanding that everything happen on your terms.","Give the day one memorable experience that is actually worth remembering."],"donts":["Don't repeat the exact same routine all day just because it is familiar.","Don't make a huge permanent promise in the middle of a temporary rush.","Don't drown the day in junk food, games, scrolling, or other quick-hit distractions.","Don't run from the conversation that still needs to be handled.","Don't trap yourself in one spot for hours if your body and mind are clearly asking for movement.","Don't blow up a stable situation just because you are bored.","Don't spend money impulsively because the experience feels exciting.","Don't confuse having options with needing to use every option.","Don't ghost a responsibility because something more interesting appeared.","Don't chase stimulation until your nervous system is fried.","Don't turn freedom into an excuse to be unreliable.","Don't assume a new person, place, or plan will fix a problem you keep carrying with you.","Don't change direction so often that nothing has time to become valuable."]},"6":{"dos":["Check on family or somebody close to you, and make the care practical.","Improve your space with something clean, useful, comfortable, or beautiful.","Take care of yourself on purpose instead of waiting until you are depleted.","Help somebody solve a problem when they actually want your help.","Drop one old grudge that is costing you more energy than it is worth.","Cook, clean, repair, or handle one thing that makes home life easier.","Tell somebody you appreciate them without attaching a lecture to it.","Ask what somebody needs before deciding what kind of help they should receive.","Spend real uninterrupted time with somebody who matters to you.","Handle one responsibility you have been quietly hoping somebody else would notice.","Make one corner of your environment feel calmer and more cared for.","Say no to one request that would push you past your real capacity.","Give yourself the same patience you keep trying to give everybody else."],"donts":["Don't insert yourself into drama that has nothing to do with you.","Don't volunteer for so much that your help turns into resentment.","Don't pick apart every little imperfection around you.","Don't turn your sacrifices into a scoreboard.","Don't take care of everybody else while ignoring your own body and emotions.","Don't fix somebody's problem before they have asked for your solution.","Don't use guilt to get cooperation.","Don't assume being needed means the relationship is healthy.","Don't clean, organize, or correct the life out of the people around you.","Don't carry a family problem alone when it clearly needs a group conversation.","Don't confuse worry with proof that something bad is happening.","Don't say yes because you are afraid somebody will think you do not care.","Don't make love conditional on people doing things exactly your way."]},"7":{"dos":["Learn something that makes you think: read, study, research, or watch something substantial.","Give yourself real quiet time with no need to perform for anybody.","Journal, meditate, think deeply, or sit with a question long enough to hear your own answer.","Take a solo walk somewhere calm if you can.","Pay attention to your gut and your body, then check what they are telling you against the facts.","Review the fine print before you agree to something important.","Take a break from unnecessary noise and let your mind settle.","Research one question deeply instead of skimming twenty answers.","Notice whether your body is asking for rest, food, water, movement, or medical attention.","Write down the facts of a worry before your imagination adds to them.","Protect one block of time for focused work with no social interruption.","Revisit a decision after you have had enough quiet to think clearly.","Choose depth over volume in what you consume today."],"donts":["Don't waste the day in shallow gossip just to fill silence.","Don't overload your head with noise, crowds, and constant input.","Don't think a simple concern into a full disaster before anything has actually happened.","Don't become suspicious of people who have given you no real reason to distrust them.","Don't ignore your inner warning signs just because everybody else seems fine with something.","Don't diagnose yourself from one random symptom and a spiral of internet searches.","Don't isolate so hard that you lose useful perspective.","Don't treat every coincidence like proof of a hidden pattern.","Don't skip food, water, sleep, or basic body care because your mind is busy.","Don't keep analyzing a decision after you already have enough information to make it.","Don't turn privacy into shutting out somebody who has earned your trust.","Don't force yourself into loud social energy if your system is clearly asking for quiet.","Don't ignore pain, sickness, injury risk, or a physical warning sign just to stay on schedule. Standing overlay: Code13 treats 7 as carrying a real sickness/injury caution. The Today layer can surface the stronger body warning separately from the rotation bank."]},"8":{"dos":["Look directly at your money: budget, savings, pricing, debt, income, or the next financial move.","Take responsibility and lead where a decision actually needs to be made.","Use some of your resources to help somebody when it makes sense.","Carry yourself like you expect your decisions to matter.","Face the business or financial choice you have been avoiding and deal with the real numbers.","Negotiate one term instead of automatically accepting what is offered.","Review where your time is producing value and where it is being wasted.","Set a concrete financial target instead of vaguely wanting more.","Follow up on the invoice, proposal, opportunity, or deal that is still open.","Make one decision that improves long-term material stability.","Put resources behind the project that has actually earned more support.","Ask whether the price, effort, and return still make sense before you continue.","Use authority to make the system cleaner, fairer, or more effective."],"donts":["Don't let scarcity talk make the decision for you.","Don't use authority as an excuse to bully or control people.","Don't spend for status just to prove that you can.","Don't shrink out of a serious opportunity because fear got loud.","Don't cheat, manipulate, or cut an ethical corner for a faster win.","Don't confuse expensive with valuable.","Don't make a money move just because your ego wants to feel powerful.","Don't turn every conversation into a negotiation.","Don't ignore the human cost of a decision because the numbers look good.","Don't take on a financial risk you have not actually calculated.","Don't chase more money without deciding what the money is for.","Don't force a deal that is showing you bad terms.","Don't start something new financially when the Code13 7-and-8 enemy exception is active. Standing exception: when the real Code13 7-and-8 enemy exception fires, normal 8 money-move guidance flips to caution around starting something new financially."]},"9":{"dos":["Clear out something you already know you are finished with.","Finish an open project before you rush to create another commitment.","Let one old conflict go if there is nothing useful left to solve.","Check that your choices still sound like you, not like the crowd around you.","Spend time around people and environments that do not drag your state downward.","Donate, delete, archive, or remove something that belongs to an old chapter.","Have the goodbye, closure, or final conversation you keep postponing when it is safe and appropriate.","Adapt the plan to what is actually happening instead of what you hoped would happen.","Return something, cancel something, or close a loop that keeps taking up mental space.","Notice whose mood you are carrying and give back what is not yours.","Finish one thing cleanly enough that you do not have to keep revisiting it.","Let new information change your position when the old position no longer fits.","Choose one relationship or environment where you can be yourself without constantly adjusting."],"donts":["Don't keep reopening an old argument just because the emotion is familiar.","Don't reshape your real opinion just to make yourself easier for a group to accept.","Don't pile a massive new long-term commitment on top of something that is trying to end.","Don't absorb everybody else's bad mood and call it your own.","Don't run from the ending, goodbye, or closure that already needs to happen.","Don't keep an object, obligation, or relationship only because you have had it a long time.","Don't confuse understanding somebody with owing them unlimited access to you.","Don't force the old plan after reality has clearly changed.","Don't spend the day reliving a version of the past you cannot return to.","Don't let somebody else's personality replace your own while you are around them.","Don't reopen a closed door just because the quiet afterward feels unfamiliar.","Don't carry emotional residue from one room into the next without checking it.","Don't make adaptation mean abandoning your own standards."]},"11":{"dos":["Write down the dream, gut hit, or sudden idea before it disappears.","Capture the weird idea first. You can decide later whether it is useful.","Use your energy to inspire somebody without needing them to copy you.","Calm your body on purpose with stretching, breathing, meditation, or quiet movement.","Notice patterns and coincidences, but stay grounded enough to test what they actually mean.","Lower unnecessary stimulation before you make an emotional decision.","Put a powerful idea into one practical next step.","Take ten quiet minutes before responding to something that hits you hard.","Write the feeling down in plain language instead of turning it into a prophecy.","Choose music, lighting, movement, or environment that helps your nervous system settle.","Talk to somebody grounded if your own thoughts are starting to loop.","Protect sleep tonight instead of treating intensity like unlimited energy.","Ask what still feels true after the emotional wave passes."],"donts":["Don't instantly dismiss a strong inner signal, but don't treat it as proof either.","Don't pour caffeine, sugar, and more stimulation on top of an already wired nervous system.","Don't sit all day in an environment that keeps draining or agitating you.","Don't kill a big idea just because it sounds impossible before you have examined it.","Don't spend the entire day looping on tiny details until the useful signal disappears.","Don't make a permanent decision in the middle of an emotional spike.","Don't treat every coincidence as a command.","Don't assume intensity automatically means accuracy.","Don't stay online feeding an anxious loop when your body clearly needs grounding.","Don't expect yourself to operate at maximum inspiration all day.","Don't turn a strong intuition into an accusation without evidence.","Don't ignore an emotional crash because the morning felt powerful.","Don't frame impure 11 as becoming a 2. Code13 keeps it as a less stable 11. Standing overlay: 11 keeps the emotional-crash / grounding warning. Impure 11 remains a less stable 11 and never becomes 2."]},"22":{"dos":["Take one concrete step that makes the big dream more real.","Map the long game in enough detail that somebody could actually follow it.","Put serious effort into work that can help more than just you.","Let yourself think at full scale before you start shrinking the idea for convenience.","Take one chaotic system and make it cleaner, simpler, and more usable.","Break a massive goal into the next three buildable stages.","Identify the bottleneck that could collapse the larger plan and deal with it early.","Put the right person, tool, or resource into the part of the system that needs it.","Write down the dependencies instead of pretending every piece can happen at once.","Protect quality on the part of the project that has to carry real weight.","Make one decision with the next year in mind instead of only the next hour.","Turn a vision statement into an actual timeline, budget, prototype, or operating plan.","Eat, rest, and maintain the body that has to execute the big plan."],"donts":["Don't make yourself think small just because the big version scares you.","Don't reduce the whole day to tiny personal wins when the work has a larger purpose.","Don't quit just because the project finally becomes difficult enough to be real.","Don't let sloppy structure wreck something that needs coordination.","Don't treat your body like a machine. Eat, rest, and keep the builder functional.","Don't make the plan so perfect that nobody can start it.","Don't expect one person to carry a system that clearly needs a team.","Don't treat people like interchangeable parts of your project.","Don't ignore a boring logistical problem because the vision is more exciting.","Don't confuse scale with complexity. Simpler can still be bigger.","Don't add another layer when the foundation underneath it is unstable.","Don't let fear of wasting your potential become the reason you never ship anything.","Don't hide the 22/4 slash state when the engine says the day is impure. Display rule: impure 22/4 must preserve the slash state."]},"28":{"dos":["Put effort into the task with the clearest path to material return.","Review what your work is actually worth before you price or negotiate it.","Finish a revenue-producing task before spending hours on cosmetic work.","Follow up on money that is already owed, pending, or available to you.","Improve one skill, system, or offer that can increase your earning power.","Choose the opportunity where value exchange is clear on both sides.","Track one number that tells you whether your effort is paying off.","Turn useful work into something sellable, billable, or materially productive.","Protect the quality of the work that your reputation or income depends on.","Ask what action creates gain because it creates value, not because it exploits somebody.","Put a portion of gain toward stability instead of immediately spending it.","Cut one expense, leak, or low-value effort that is eating the return.","Define what enough looks like before the pursuit of more takes over."],"donts":["Don't chase money through a shortcut that destroys the value underneath it.","Don't let greed turn a good opportunity into a bad decision.","Don't confuse a higher price with a better deal.","Don't take more from an exchange than the value honestly supports.","Don't spend the whole day fantasizing about gain without doing the work that creates it.","Don't keep increasing the target just because the last target was reached.","Don't risk something essential for a gain you have not properly measured.","Don't hide bad terms behind excitement about the possible payout.","Don't treat people like wallets, leads, or numbers only.","Don't let material success become the only evidence you use to judge the day.","Don't underprice real work out of fear and then resent the exchange afterward.","Don't spend new gain immediately just to prove that you made it.","Don't let 'more' become the plan when you have not decided what the money is for. Doctrine boundary: unlike the other roots, the supplied source did not contain a dedicated 28 Universal Day action plan. All 26 lines here are new Code13 production copy derived only from the established fixed doctrine: effort -> material gain, with greed as the shadow."]},"33":{"dos":["Teach or guide somebody with patience instead of showing off what you know.","Do one useful act of kindness that does not need recognition.","Put some warmth into the room: encouragement, humor, praise, or genuine support.","Protect your own emotional space while you are helping other people.","Speak up for somebody who genuinely needs support and has less power in the situation.","Ask somebody what would actually help before you decide how to save them.","Share knowledge in a way that makes the other person more capable.","Take care of one emotional need of your own before you become everybody else's support line.","Encourage somebody without making their outcome your responsibility.","Use your influence to calm a situation instead of making yourself the center of it.","Set one compassionate boundary that protects your ability to keep showing up.","Make something uplifting, useful, or healing without forcing it to be profound.","Leave one person stronger, clearer, or more confident than you found them."],"donts":["Don't flood yourself with everybody else's pain until you cannot function.","Don't demand perfection from imperfect people because your standards are high.","Don't neglect your own health just to prove how much you can carry.","Don't let somebody else's bitterness decide how you behave.","Don't keep announcing the weight you carry. Set the boundary or change the load.","Don't rescue somebody from a consequence they need in order to learn.","Don't confuse being needed with being loved.","Don't make somebody feel guilty because they did not use your advice.","Don't absorb every tragic story you see and carry it like a personal assignment.","Don't let public responsibility erase the people closest to you.","Don't keep helping after your help has clearly become control.","Don't martyr yourself for a problem nobody asked you to own.","Don't hide the 33/6 slash state when the engine says the day is impure. Display rule: impure 33/6 must preserve the slash state."]}};
C13B.bank04verdict = {"peak":{"signals":["Today's {day} energy locks in hard with your {person} side.","Today's {day} energy gives your {person} side a very clean lane.","Your {person} side has unusually strong support from today's {day} energy.","Today's {day} current and your {person} side are working with each other, not around each other."],"meaning":["Do not waste the fit. Put this part of yourself on something that matters.","The day is giving this side of you room to operate with less resistance than usual.","This is the kind of alignment that can make the right move feel cleaner and easier to execute.","Use the support for something concrete. Strong compatibility matters most when it turns into action."],"action":["Give this side of you the lead on one important move.","Use the opening on something measurable before the day gets noisy.","Choose one meaningful target and act while the lane is clean.","Put the alignment into motion instead of only noticing that the day feels good."]},"good":{"signals":["Today's {day} energy works well with your {person} side.","Your {person} side has a good lane through today's {day} energy.","Today's {day} current supports the way your {person} side naturally moves.","There is real cooperation between today's {day} energy and your {person} side."],"meaning":["Lean into the clean version of this side of yourself. The day is more likely to reward it than fight it.","You do not need to force the fit. Use what already feels natural and keep it practical.","This side of you has useful support today. Give it a real job instead of leaving it as a mood.","The fit is strong enough to trust, but it still needs a decision from you."],"action":["Use this side of yourself on the task that fits it best.","Make one move that matches the strength of this pairing.","Let this side lead where it already has support.","Take the clean opportunity instead of overcomplicating it."]},"mid":{"signals":["Today's {day} energy is workable with your {person} side, but it is not doing the work for you.","Your {person} side can use today's {day} energy, but the fit is not automatic.","Today's {day} current sits in the middle with your {person} side. There is room to work with it.","This pairing is steady rather than extreme. Your {person} side has to choose how to use the day."],"meaning":["Nothing is badly broken here, but nothing is carrying you either. Stay deliberate.","This is not a warning and it is not a green light. Use judgment and keep the day simple.","The middle tier means the pairing can go either way depending on how cleanly you handle it.","Treat this as usable energy, not automatic momentum."],"action":["Keep the move simple and check the result before you add more.","Use the day, but do not overread it.","Make the practical choice and leave room to adjust.","Stay flexible. This pairing responds better to judgment than force."]},"clash":{"signals":["Today's {day} energy clashes with your {person} side.","Today's {day} current pushes against the way your {person} side naturally wants to move.","Your {person} side has real friction with today's {day} energy.","Today's {day} energy and your {person} side are pulling in different directions."],"meaning":["Do not force your default move just because it usually works. The day is asking for adjustment.","Friction is the signal. Slow down enough to see where your normal instinct is making the situation harder.","This does not mean the whole day is bad. It means this side of you needs more control and less autopilot.","Use the warning early. A small adjustment now is cheaper than pushing through resistance all day."],"action":["Pause before the move you would normally make on autopilot.","Use the opposite skill for a minute: more patience, more structure, more space, or more restraint.","Do not turn friction into a bigger fight than it needs to be.","Adjust the approach before you abandon the goal."]},"quiet":{"signals":["Nothing is screaming for attention here. Your {person} side can stay steady and work the day without forcing a story onto it.","This is a quieter pairing. Let your {person} side do its job without treating every small shift like a sign.","The day is not heavily pushing or blocking your {person} side. Steady is enough.","Your {person} side does not need a dramatic verdict today. Keep it clean and keep moving. MIXED DAY CONNECTORS","One part of the day is opening while another is pushing back. Treat them as two separate instructions.","Today is mixed, not confused. Use the supportive lane and respect the friction lane.","You have a green light in one place and resistance in another. Do not average them into one vague mood.","The day is giving you both leverage and a warning. Use each where it actually belongs. Mixed means one eligible personal pair is good and the other is bad. They stay as two findings. The connector explains structure only; it never claims a new psychological relationship. Production Assembly Pattern SIGNAL -> PERSON MEANING -> CONCRETE SCENE -> ACTION","SIGNAL comes from this bank and is selected only after the real score is known.","PERSON MEANING comes from Bank 01. Good/peak uses the person's light pool. Clash uses the person's shadow pool. Mid can use a restrained light or neutral identity line without pretending the pair is strong.","CONCRETE SCENE comes from Bank 01 and cannot repeat for the same root inside one reading.","ACTION comes from Bank 03. The Universal Day always owns the lead Do and Don't. A featured pair can add a supporting line only under the existing composer rules. Example shape, not a hardcoded pair claim: Today's {day archetype} energy clashes with your {person archetype} side. [Pull one real shadow line for the person's root.] Think: [pull one scene]. [Pull/bridge one eligible action.] Numerology Table - Production Reference Direction matters: row = entity/person side, column = day side. The same two roots can score differently when reversed. 13 borrows 4's row and column. Impure 22/4 and 33/6 look up through the companion but keep the slash in display. 11 never becomes 2. ROW\\DAY GOOD GOOD MID MID MID MID PEAK GOOD CLASH PEAK MID GOOD MID GOOD MID GOOD MID MID MID MID PEAK CLASH MID MID GOOD MID MID GOOD GOOD CLASH PEAK GOOD MID PEAK MID GOOD MID GOOD GOOD MID GOOD CLASH GOOD CLASH PEAK GOOD GOOD GOOD MID MID MID MID MID MID PEAK CLASH PEAK CLASH GOOD GOOD GOOD MID CLASH MID PEAK MID MID GOOD PEAK CLASH MID CLASH GOOD GOOD MID GOOD MID MID PEAK MID MID GOOD GOOD CLASH MID CLASH MID PEAK GOOD PEAK MID GOOD PEAK PEAK GOOD GOOD GOOD CLASH CLASH MID MID PEAK PEAK PEAK CLASH CLASH MID GOOD GOOD GOOD MID MID CLASH CLASH CLASH CLASH CLASH PEAK MID GOOD MID MID MID PEAK MID CLASH MID MID MID MID MID MID MID MID CLASH GOOD GOOD PEAK CLASH MID MID MID MID PEAK GOOD GOOD MID MID MID GOOD PEAK CLASH MID MID GOOD MID MID MID GOOD MID PEAK MID MID PEAK CLASH MID MID MID MID Archetype Token Map 1: Pioneer 2: Peacemaker 3: Storyteller 4: Builder 5: Explorer 6: Caretaker 7: Seeker 8: Executive 9: Mirror 11: Antenna 22: Master Builder 28: Wealth-Builder 33: Guardian The token map is for assembly. Narrative output should not expose lookup mechanics or numeric table cells."]}};
C13B.bank05 = {"body7":{"trigger":"Universal Day resolves to 7, or the existing Today logic explicitly calls the standing 7 warning.","doctrine":"Code13 treats 7 as a real body-watch day. The source language says to watch the body because sickness or injury risk is part of the house guidance. This is a caution, not a diagnosis or guaranteed prediction.","lines":["Your body gets a louder vote today. If something feels off, do not bulldoze through it just to stay on schedule.","Keep the day a little cleaner physically. Rest, hydration, food, and basic awareness matter more than pretending you can run on fumes.","Today is not the day to ignore a physical warning sign because the rest of the plan looks inconvenient.","Move with a little more awareness than usual. The 7 pattern asks you to notice strain before strain has to shout.","Your mind may want to keep analyzing while your body is asking for something simpler: rest, food, water, quiet, or recovery.","Treat small physical signals like information, not drama. You do not need to panic, but you also do not need to dismiss them.","Slow down enough to notice how you are actually feeling. A 7 day rewards attention more than stubbornness.","Be careful with the 'I'm fine' autopilot today. If your body keeps repeating the same message, listen.","Protect your energy physically. Overloading the day just to prove you can handle it misses the point of the warning.","Give yourself margin. Rushing, exhaustion, and ignoring your limits are a bad combination under this pattern.","If you feel run-down, adjust the plan instead of turning the day into a test of toughness.","Keep the body check practical: sleep, food, water, movement, pain, fatigue. Notice what is real before your mind invents a story.","The warning is simple: pay attention to your body today. Awareness is useful; fear is not."],"title":"7 DAY \u00b7 BODY / HEALTH CAUTION"},"enemy78":{"trigger":"The active Code13 Today pairing hits the established 7-and-8 enemy exception.","doctrine":"Normal 8-day money-move guidance flips. Under this exception, Code13 says not to start something new financially. This overlay overrides ordinary 8 encouragement around new financial moves.","lines":["This is not the clean 8 money window. If the 7-and-8 exception is active, protect the position before you create a new one.","Normally 8 says move on the money. Not here. Review, verify, and hold off on launching a new financial commitment.","The money signal flips under this pairing. Use the day to inspect the deal, not to rush into it.","Keep financial decisions defensive today. Check terms, numbers, timing, and hidden assumptions before you add anything new.","The 8 wants action, but the 7 is throwing scrutiny into the lane. Let scrutiny win before new money goes out.","Do not confuse financial pressure with a deadline. If the decision can wait, give yourself more information first.","Use the money energy for cleanup: review expenses, collect information, reconcile numbers, or close an existing loop. Avoid opening a fresh risk.","This pairing is better for due diligence than expansion. Read the fine print before you make the move.","If a new deal needs you to ignore a question mark, that is the question mark to investigate.","Do not let ambition bully caution today. The exception exists because this combination can make a money move look cleaner than it is.","Pause the new financial start. You can still plan, price, research, and negotiate without committing the whole position.","Treat today's money decisions like an audit. What holds up after scrutiny is more useful than what looks exciting at first.","The clean play is restraint. Protect capital, verify the facts, and let the next move earn your confidence."],"title":"7 \u2194 8 \u00b7 FINANCIAL ENEMY EXCEPTION"},"crash11":{"trigger":"Universal Day resolves to 11, or the Today logic calls the standing 11 emotional warning.","doctrine":"Code13 treats 11 as emotionally intense. The established warning is to watch for an emotional crash and ground the feeling first. Strong feeling is not automatically accurate information.","lines":["Your emotional volume can run high today. Feel it, but do not let the first wave make every decision for you.","11 can make a real signal feel huge and a small signal feel huge too. Ground first, interpret second.","If the morning feels electric, do not assume you can run at that voltage all day. Leave room for the drop.","Strong intuition is worth noticing today. It is still worth checking after your nervous system settles.","Watch the swing from inspired to drained. Intensity is not an unlimited fuel source.","Before you send the emotional message, make the permanent decision, or call something destiny, give your body time to calm down.","Lower unnecessary stimulation. More caffeine, more noise, and more scrolling can turn useful sensitivity into static.","You may pick up more than usual today. Not everything you feel belongs to you, and not everything you notice needs an immediate response.","Capture the idea while it is hot. Make the decision when you are grounded.","If your emotions suddenly crash, treat that as a cue to regulate, not as proof that everything you believed earlier was wrong.","The 11 warning is not 'do not feel.' It is 'do not confuse emotional force with certainty.'","Protect your sleep and your nervous system tonight. A high-voltage day gets expensive when you keep feeding it after the useful part is over.","Ask one question before acting on a strong feeling: does this still make sense when I am calm?"],"title":"11 DAY \u00b7 EMOTIONAL OVERLOAD / CRASH"},"impure11":{"trigger":"The engine identifies an impure 11 state.","doctrine":"Impure 11 remains 11. It is a less stable 11 and never becomes or oscillates into 2.","lines":["This is still 11 energy, just less stable. The signal can be real while the interpretation moves around.","Your sensitivity may be sharp today, but the confidence attached to it can change fast. Write it down before you act on it.","Impure 11 can make inspiration and overwhelm sit too close together. Give the idea somewhere to land before the emotion runs away with it.","Do not reduce this into a softer 2 story. Code13 keeps the 11 intact and treats the instability as part of the reading.","The antenna is picking things up, but the reception may flicker. Separate what you noticed from the story you immediately built around it.","You may move between clarity and doubt faster than usual. That does not mean either state deserves total control.","Keep your interpretation provisional. A strong hit can be worth recording without becoming a final conclusion.","Impure 11 needs grounding more than certainty. Slow the nervous system down before you decide what the signal means.","Expect more fluctuation around mood, confidence, or interpretation. Keep the practical next step small enough to survive that fluctuation.","Do not chase a stable feeling by adding more stimulation. Less input can make the actual signal easier to hear.","Let the insight repeat before you build around it. One intense moment does not have to become the whole story.","The useful version of this state is sensitivity with verification. Notice first. Test second.","Keep the label honest: 11, less stable. Never 2."],"title":"IMPURE 11 \u00b7 LESS-STABLE ANTENNA"},"impure22":{"trigger":"The engine produces an impure 22/4 state.","doctrine":"Code13 preserves the slash. Impure 22/4 oscillates between the 22 pattern and its companion 4 pattern.","lines":["22/4 can make you think at full scale one minute and obsess over the next brick the next. Both sides are part of the state.","The big vision is real, and so is the pull toward control, detail, and structure. Use the 4 side to build the 22 side instead of letting them fight.","If the project suddenly feels too large, come back to the next concrete piece. That is not abandoning the vision; that is how this state stabilizes it.","Watch the swing between 'this could be huge' and 'nothing is ready enough.' The slash state can turn ambition into paralysis if perfection gets the final vote.","22/4 works best when the vision has a floor under it. Put one system, deadline, budget, or sequence beneath the idea.","You may feel pulled between scale and safety. Do not shrink the goal just to calm the discomfort; give the goal better structure.","The 4 side can rescue the 22 from overwhelm, but it can also trap it in endless preparation. Build something real before you build another plan.","Keep the slash visible in the reading because the instability matters. This is not a pure 22 pretending to be consistent.","Use the large-scale instinct to choose the direction. Use the Builder side to decide what gets done today.","Control is the trap when uncertainty rises. Structure is useful; trying to control every moving piece is not.","If ordinary progress starts feeling embarrassingly small, remember that the big thing still has to be built out of small things.","Do not let the pressure of potential make you freeze. A functioning first layer beats a perfect imaginary system.","The clean 22/4 move is simple: keep the big architecture, then earn it one stable piece at a time."],"title":"IMPURE 22/4 \u00b7 MASTER BUILDER OSCILLATION"},"impure33":{"trigger":"The engine produces an impure 33/6 state.","doctrine":"Code13 preserves the slash. Impure 33/6 oscillates between the 33 pattern and its companion 6 pattern.","lines":["33/6 can pull you between helping at a larger scale and taking care of the people right in front of you. Neither side is fake.","Your influence may want to reach outward while your Caretaker side keeps noticing what needs attention at home. The job is balance, not choosing a morally superior side.","The slash state can make responsibility feel endless. Decide what is actually yours before compassion turns into overload.","You may move between teacher mode and caretaker mode today. Help in the form the situation actually needs, not the form that makes you feel most useful.","33 wants impact. 6 wants care. The clean version makes the impact caring and the care sustainable.","Watch the guilt trap. A wider mission does not excuse neglecting close relationships, and close responsibility does not mean you must abandon the larger calling.","If everybody seems to need something from you, that is exactly when boundaries become part of the service.","Keep the slash visible. This state can genuinely swing between broad influence and personal responsibility.","Do not prove your compassion by exhausting yourself. A burnt-out Guardian is not more helpful because the sacrifice looked noble.","The 6 side can keep the 33 human. The 33 side can keep the 6 from shrinking its care into only the familiar circle.","Notice when helping turns into rescuing. The unstable state can make being needed feel like evidence that you are doing the right thing.","Let care strengthen other people's agency. If your support makes them more dependent on you, the shadow is taking over.","The clean 33/6 move is to help at the right scale without abandoning your own needs or the people closest to you."],"title":"IMPURE 33/6 \u00b7 GUARDIAN / CARETAKER OSCILLATION"},"greed28":{"trigger":"A 28 wealth pattern is active and the copy layer needs a shadow or caution overlay.","doctrine":"28 is a fixed wealth number, not a master number. Its supported meaning is effort converting to material gain, with greed as the established shadow.","lines":["28 can reward real effort, but the shadow starts when 'more' becomes the goal with no definition of enough.","Keep the value exchange clean. Material gain is strongest here when the work underneath it is actually useful.","If the opportunity only works because somebody else gets squeezed unfairly, that is the greed shadow, not the wealth pattern working well.","Do not move the target every time you hit it. Decide what the gain is for before the pursuit becomes automatic.","28 wants effort to convert. It does not say every possible dollar is worth chasing.","Check whether the next money move improves stability or only feeds appetite.","The clean question is not 'how much can I get?' It is 'what value am I creating, and what return actually makes sense?'","Material progress can be real without becoming your only scoreboard.","Watch the moment ambition stops being attached to usefulness. That is where the 28 shadow starts getting expensive.","Protect the reputation, relationship, or system that produces the gain. Short-term extraction can wreck the thing that was making money possible.","Do not underprice yourself from fear, and do not overreach from greed. Keep the exchange honest.","Let some of the gain become stability. If every win immediately creates a bigger appetite, the number is running you.","28 works best when effort, value, and return stay connected."],"title":"28 \u00b7 GREED SHADOW / WEALTH CHECK"}};
